# No git commits from Cursor

Do **not** run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or any other command that creates or rewrites commits in this repository.

- Do not commit changes unless the user explicitly asks you to commit in that specific message.
- If the user asks to "save" or "apply" work, stage or edit files only — do not commit.
- If a workflow would normally end with a commit (e.g. after a feature is done), stop after the code changes and tell the user they can commit manually.
- You may still run read-only git commands (`git status`, `git diff`, `git log`) when needed for context.

This rule applies only to the PaduchuAndham project.
